<figure class="safe-read" aria-labelledby="r28-safe-title">
 <figcaption id="r28-safe-title"><span>Figure 2</span> Both partitions must be safe at the chosen timestamp</figcaption>
 <safe-snapshot>
  <div class="controls"><label>Read timestamp <select data-time><option value="100">100 · before purchase</option><option value="115">115 · after purchase</option></select></label><label>B’s safe applied history <select data-progress><option value="105">Through 105 · behind</option><option value="120">Through 120 · caught up</option></select></label></div>
  <p class="history">100: before purchase → 110: purchase commits → 115: later read → 120</p>
  <div class="parts"><div><strong>A · stock replica</strong><p>Safe through 120</p><p data-stock></p></div><div><strong>B · order replica</strong><p data-progress-label>Safe through 105</p><p data-order></p></div></div>
  <p class="result" data-result aria-live="polite"></p>
 </safe-snapshot>
 <p class="caption">An illustrative timestamp model. The numbers order database history; they are not milliseconds or wall-clock readings. A safe frontier means the replica has the required history applied and the protocol guarantees no still-unresolved write can later change the answer at or below it. Retention is assumed sufficient.</p>
 <details><summary>Read the four cases</summary><p>At 100, both replicas can answer even while B is safe only through 105: stock 1, no order 103. At 115, A can answer stock 0 but B cannot safely complete its portion while safe only through 105. Once B is safe through 120, the combined answer at 115 is stock 0 and pending order 103. Catching B up does not change the chosen answer at 100.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 import {commonRead} from './read.mjs';
 class SafeSnapshot extends HTMLElement{
  connectedCallback(){if(this.dataset.ready)return;this.dataset.ready='true';const time=this.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-time]')!;const progress=this.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-progress]')!;const draw=()=>{const s=commonRead(Number(time.value),Number(progress.value));this.querySelector('[data-stock]')!.textContent=`At ${s.timestamp}: P7 stock ${s.stock}`;this.querySelector('[data-progress-label]')!.textContent=`Safe through ${s.bSafe}`;this.querySelector('[data-order]')!.textContent=s.safe?`At ${s.timestamp}: ${s.order}`:`Cannot certify timestamp ${s.timestamp}`;this.querySelector('[data-result]')!.textContent=s.safe?`Complete common snapshot at ${s.timestamp}: P7 stock ${s.stock}; ${s.order}.`:`No complete result at ${s.timestamp}. Wait for B, route to a replica that can serve that timestamp, or explicitly choose an older snapshot for the whole read.`;};time.addEventListener('change',draw);progress.addEventListener('change',draw);draw();}
 }
 if(!customElements.get('safe-snapshot'))customElements.define('safe-snapshot',SafeSnapshot);
</script>
<style>
